# Frozen, SHRINK-ONLY allowlist of lib/*.sh files with no production caller.
#
# A file here is dead code: nothing under lib/, scripts/ or pl references it.
# It is tolerated only because removing it is a separate decision with its own
# blast radius — NOT because it works.
#
# RULES
#   * NEVER add a line to this file. tests/unit/test-host.bats asserts the
#     count is <= 6 and fails if a new dead lib appears.
#   * Removing a line (by deleting the file or giving it a real caller) is
#     always welcome and requires no ceremony.
#   * A file named in CLAUDE.md may NEVER be allowlisted — the standing orders
#     must not point at code that does not run. That rule is what retired
#     lib/safe-ops.sh: CLAUDE.md told agents to `source` it, it had zero
#     callers, and it printed the names of root scripts that do not exist
#     (./stg2prod.sh, ./backup.sh), so dead code read as coverage.
#
# Frozen 2026-07-26 at 6 entries (was 7; safe-ops.sh deleted by item 6).

lib/developer.sh
lib/live-server-setup.sh
lib/llm.sh
lib/timezone.sh
lib/todo-autolog.sh
lib/verify-opportunistic.sh
